$\boxed{A_5\text{ is not a nontrivial free product}.}$ If $g\ne1$ and $h\ne1$ belong to different factors, the powers $(gh)^r$ have distinct normal forms of length $2r$. Every <nontrivial free product> is therefore an <infinite group>, whereas the <alternating group> $A_5$ is a <finite group> of order $60$.

