Eliminate $t$ using $t=xsx^{-1}$. The remaining relation $xtx^{-1}=s$ becomes $x^2sx^{-2}=s$, which follows from $x^2=1$. These <Tietze transformations> give
$$
\boxed{G\cong\langle x,s\mid x^2=1\rangle\cong C_2*\mathbb Z.}
$$
Both factors are nontrivial, so this is a <nontrivial free product>. Conversely, in $C_2*\langle s\rangle$ the definition $t=xsx^{-1}$ satisfies both conjugation relations, confirming that eliminating $t$ loses no relation.

